title: Spec v3.5 and PR-0 landed; kernel-linking design (31/32) awaits founder rulings
summary: |-
  Spec v3.5 is written: K1–K8, D68–D72, and the merged 15-probe M1.0 table with a runs-on column. K7 judgment: a re-used launch token within its 60 s TTL is theft and revokes; after the TTL it is refused and logged only. PR-0 scaffold is committed at 3b93de64, green locally (56 tests, fence and SEC mutation-checked; Windows/Ubuntu CI unverified until pushed).

  Kernel linking: Arky (31) and Aegis (32) agree on a separate gnomon-link:v1 peer protocol (peers never reach the 12 verbs), Noise over node:crypto with a new link key, root-presence pairing on both sides with SAS, handoff fencing (seal before the bundle leaves, custody epoch, cards re-raised on the target), pull-only co-work through a cowork mod with inject receipts, and egress by audience/sensitivity.

  They differ on transport:
  - Arky: outbound-only kernels with a self-hosted blind relay on the home server.
  - Aegis: direct LAN allowed on named interfaces, mDNS as a hint only.

  The earliest honest slice is M2.8, own-machines handoff, after Move 1 passes. Move 1 must reserve contract values and label sensitivity correctly from day one.

  Founder questions: amend the §1 non-goals; relay host/overlay; teammate handoff and subscription (OPEN 7); Warpline-mode handoff.
